    Reinier Maliepaard, Martin Tarenskeen, Paul Villiger,
    Alexander Scheutzow, Herbert Schneider, David Randolph,
    Michael Strasser

    This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it
    under the terms of the Lesser GNU General Public License as published by
    the Free Software Foundation.

    This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but
    WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
    MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the Lesser GNU
    General Public License for more details.

    <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl.html>

That notice is reproduced verbatim from the header of abc2xml.py itself,
which is authoritative. Canonical source and full documentation:

    https://wim.vree.org/svgParse/abc2xml.html

abc2xml.py is VENDORED here, not forked: this repository has no upstream
remote and shares no history with Willem Vree's. It carries house
modifications (a glob-metacharacter fix, MusicXML conformance and Dorico
enum work, and the D116 performance-tag guard); the `.pre-*` snapshots
beside it record the state before each. Those modifications are likewise
LGPL, being derivative of an LGPL work.

